// NeoMIFES executable resources (WI-07 step10).
//
// Icon only - deliberately does NOT embed an application manifest here.
// main.cpp already requests the Common Controls v6 side-by-side assembly
// via a `#pragma comment(linker, "/manifestdependency:...")` (see that
// file's own comment), which the linker's default `/MANIFEST` behavior
// merges into the auto-generated manifest resource (RT_MANIFEST, resource
// ID 1) at link time. Defining a second RT_MANIFEST resource here (ID 1)
// would collide with that linker-generated one - so the "MANIFESTINPUT vs.
// MANIFEST:NO" choice this step's plan flagged as needing a pre-
// implementation probe turned out to be moot: this .rc simply never
// touches RT_MANIFEST at all, leaving the existing, already-proven
// pragma-based manifest untouched.
//
// The icon itself is a placeholder (solid background + "N" glyph,
// generated via a throwaway PowerShell + System.Drawing script - see
// resources/neomifes.ico's own git history) - formal design tracked
// separately, see docs/issues/.
101 ICON "neomifes.ico"
